# What `agentengine build` uploads to the platform.
#
# The repository root is the agent workspace, so without this file the source
# archive would carry the whole repo: the docs, the test suite and the seed
# data, none of which the agent runs on.
# The rule here is deny-everything-at-the-top-level, then name what ships.
#
# gitignore syntax. A negation cannot resurrect a file whose parent directory is
# excluded, which is why the first line is `/*` (top-level entries only) rather
# than `*`: each directory below is re-included whole.
#
# .env, .env.*, *.pem, *.key, .git and the credential stores are excluded by the
# CLI unconditionally and cannot be negated back in.

/*

# The agent contract and the local-dev overrides.
!/agent.yaml
!/dev.yaml
!/.agentengineignore

# Build inputs. pyproject.toml declares readme = "README.md", so the README has
# to ship or the wheel build fails.
#
# No uv.lock ships. One does exist locally, written in-container by `uv sync`,
# but it is gitignored and the `/*` rule above already excludes it: nothing
# below negates it back in, so leaving it out takes no extra rule.
#
# Keeping it out is deliberate, not incidental. Both the hosted builder and the
# dev runner install the SDK from wheels baked into their base images rather
# than from an index, so a lock resolved anywhere else describes a different
# set of packages. The runner runs `uv sync --frozen` whenever a lock is
# present, which would install that set and nothing else. The scaffold ships no
# lock either; without one the builder resolves from pyproject.toml.
!/pyproject.toml
!/uv.toml
!/.python-version
!/README.md

# The agent itself.
!/mongodb_agent_engine/

# Imported by the two tools: retrieval, spanio, and their closure of clients,
# config, config_store and models. The rest of the package is Temporal ingest
# machinery the agent never imports, but it ships anyway because
# [tool.hatch.build.targets.wheel] lists the package as a whole.
!/pipeline/

# Listed in [tool.hatch.build.targets.wheel]. Nothing at runtime imports it, but
# the wheel build fails if a listed package is missing from the archive.
!/infra/

# Caches that would otherwise ride along inside the directories above.
__pycache__/
*.pyc
.pytest_cache/
.ruff_cache/
